  "text": "This prospective, multicenter phase II study evaluated the efficacy and safety of ICI combined with Hybrid-RT in patients with metastatic driver gene-negative NSCLC. Hybrid-RT is selected based on individual lesions. It adopts a dose-fractionation regimen characterized by short-course, low-total-dose radiotherapy. This approach theoretically reduces toxicity to organs at risk and minimizes radiation-induced immunosuppression, making it more suitable for combination with ICI therapy 5, 36, 37. The study met its primary endpoint, with a 1-year PFS rate of 54.2% and a median PFS of 16.1 months, representing clinically meaningful and highly promising outcomes."
